---
metadata:
  title: "Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens: Her Story | A Novel by Annie Elliot"
  description: "Discover the untold story of Mrs Dickens. Annie Elliot's historical novel reveals the life of Catherine Dickens, the woman behind the famous author."
  canonical: "https://annieelliot.co.uk/"
  pageType: "book"
---

<section id="about" class="u-container">
	<h1>Mr & Mrs Charles Dickens: <span>Her Story...</span></h1>
	<h2>So the world may know he loved me once</h2>
	<div class="amazon-tagline">
		<a
			href="https://www.amazon.co.uk/Mr-Mrs-Charles-Dickens-Story/dp/1915023742/ref=sr_1_1?crid=270O064P2TK7C&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.kAiRe4xWtUNTTwN6v8GjhbffdpBDO1i9m8UpVQ3Z9Z01mK0cJUU7nGofZTiCFXB-jSZld8S4IfYYgiqFxuFEEktK02ARb_XFVqbq7hUJQoTeN4h1obcSi3SehwWwd8vTmK_1WX_dkspf_9PBTedkn4EiN5BjNgcyWEI_LYWZpaDC1x_pxicUQcuXS5syMVxW.qabpfl6DN4IDnXciDd6PxqrdJAun147XxpHIpZqC2-0&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Mr+and+Mrs+Charles+Dickens%3A+Her+Story&amp;qid=1765401088&amp;sprefix=mr+and+mrs+charles+dickens+her+story%2Caps%2C291&amp;sr=8-1"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer"
		>
			<span class="stars">★★★★★</span> 5 stars on amazon
		</a>
	</div>
	<div>
		<div class="u-grid main-grid">
			<div>
				<p>
					After twenty-two years of marriage, the world-famous author banished
					Mrs Dickens (Catherine) from their home with their nine children and
					wrecked her reputation to protect his own when he fell in love with an
					eighteen-year-old actress.
				</p>

				<p>
					This is Kate's story: a poignant self-portrait of a woman struggling
					to achieve peace of mind by making sense of a marriage that defined,
					but nearly destroyed her. Sifting through her husband's letters after
					his sudden death she relives the happy times they shared but also
					speaks up for herself to expose the darker side of the man the world
					reveres.
				</p>

				<p>
					On her deathbed, Kate asked her daughter to give Charles's letters to
					the British Museum 'so the world may know he loved me once.' This
					novel fulfils her dying wish and restores her to history as more than
					a famous author's discarded wife. It bestows on Kate the respect,
					dignity, agency and voice she was denied in life.
				</p>

				<div class="button-container">
